
# HG changeset patch
# User Welpy-cw <58345540+Welpy-cw@users.noreply.github.com>
# Date 1786700634 -7200
# Node ID f582b42e83e54e294df46d8a0d669d7aa0db0e61
# Parent  4ffa59409972b2b3cf82e144e2700b630c4fdb64
Bug 520437 - Don't leave a duplicate summary file behind when subscribing to an IMAP folder. r=mkmelin

Subscribing to an IMAP folder that isn't on disk yet used to create an
empty summary (.msf) file as a side effect. Building the subscribe URL
reads folder info - the hierarchy delimiter in ChangeFolderSubscription
and modseq/UID state in SetupWithUrl - and those info reads went through
ReadDBFolderInfo()/GetDBFolderInfoAndDB(), which open the summary
database and create it if missing. When discovery later creates the real
summary file, the premature empty one is renamed with a "-1" suffix
(leaving a NotOnDisk-1.msf duplicate behind) or ends up orphaned.

The hierarchy delimiter is a folder-cache property (hierDelim), not a
database property, so GetHierarchyDelimiter() doesn't need the database
at all. Add a cacheOnly mode to ReadDBFolderInfo() that only reads the
folder cache and never opens or creates a summary file, and use it in
GetHierarchyDelimiter(). SetupWithUrl() only needs to peek at existing
database state, so switch it to OpenFolderDB() instead of
GetDBFolderInfoAndDB().

Add a regression test that subscribes to a folder that isn't on disk yet
and verifies that discovery creates exactly one summary file for it,
without a "-1" duplicate left behind.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317843

